# What `gcloud builds submit .` uploads as the build context.
#
# Without this file gcloud falls back to .gitignore, which mostly works — but
# relying on that couples the build context to git bookkeeping. Spelled out here
# instead, because one entry differs in a way that matters: data/clips MUST go up.
# backend/Dockerfile bakes those 20 clips in, and an image without them serves a
# play button that 404s on every archive hit.

.git
.gitignore
.gcloudignore

# Never upload secrets. Cloud Run gets these from Secret Manager and
# --set-env-vars, never from a file in the image.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Rebuilt inside the container; uploading them wastes minutes and risks shipping
# Windows-built artifacts into a Linux image.
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/

# The frontend deploys to Vercel, not into this image.
frontend/

# Pipeline inputs and local tooling: not used at runtime.
data/captions/
data/*.jsonl
docs/
scripts/
.agents/
.claude/
.shots/
skills-lock.json
rushes-blueprint.md
